665514658,2026-10-01 05:49:11,Yodatrader1,2023-04-25,19,0,,"$MU Q4: revenue $54.2B (+379% YoY) vs ~$51.1B est. Non-GAAP EPS $33.42 vs $31.61 est. Gross margin 87%. Guided Q1 FY27 to $61.5B, even higher. Behind it: 16 &quot;Strategic Customer Agreements,&quot; ~$100B in locked-in revenue through 2030. MU trades ~7x forward earnings vs $NVDA&#39;s ~15x despite similar revenue visibility. Still open: an antitrust suit vs $MU, Samsung, SK Hynix over DRAM supply restriction, unresolved by tonight&#39;s print either way. Full breakdown: https://coronetberkley.com/research/micron-memory-supercycle-earnings.html Education, not advice"
665514689,2026-10-01 05:50:31,AlphaCharge,2021-04-13,14,5,,"$MU may be one of the most dramatically undervalued AI semiconductor plays right now. The key number: an estimated 2027 P/E (KGV) of only around 7. That valuation looks striking for a company benefiting directly from explosive AI-driven demand for HBM and advanced memory. Micron just delivered exceptional growth and guided the next quarter even higher, while most of its 2027 HBM supply is already contracted. DRAM and NAND supply is also expected to remain tight, supporting pricing and profitability. A P/E of ~7 alongside this level of earnings growth, cash generation and AI exposure creates a remarkable valuation disconnect. If earnings expectations hold, the market may eventually have to reprice $MU significantly higher. Analyst target upgrades could provide another catalyst. $NVDA $AVGO $AMD"
