666089485,2026-10-08 14:45:22,SkinnyDipping,2025-06-27,248,2,,"$SPY $QQQ $NVDA $AMD Here’s some important context on the OpenAI headline that just slammed AI/semis: OpenAI did NOT suddenly cut revenue from $70B to $50B. Revenue grew by 70%. The new documents indicate OpenAI’s actual annualized revenue run rate was closer to ~$30B in July and approaching ~$50B by the end of September — meaning revenue grew 70%+ in roughly one quarter. The ~$70B figure circulating previously was an adjusted investor/media estimate that tried to make OpenAI’s revenue comparable with Anthropic’s accounting. But “OpenAI revenue collapsed” is simply not what happened. The market saw $50B vs. the previously reported investor/media estimate $70B, dumped nearly every AI-infrastructure proxy at once, and is hopefully now has started recovering as the details were digested. $30B → $50B in ~3 months is still extraordinary growth. Big difference between an AI-demand collapse and Wall Street realizing its comparison number was wrong. 😳"
